al_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6 and 833889aec024b792b1c5ce5089eaebc5eb45692f\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable unknown - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 09 Feb 2026 17:16:33 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - KDE Plasma Version: 6.5.5, KDE Frameworks Version: 6.23.0, Qt Version: 6.10.2, Graphics Platform: Wayland\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using native Wayland with KDE (Klipper as clipboard manager), copying text from the editor or in-game works for the first attempt; however, subsequent copies are not logged in the clipboard history until you copy text from another application and then copy text in Godot again.\n\nExample scenario :\n1. Copy text \"A\" inside the Godot editor\n2. Check the clipboard history, initially showing \"A\" in the list\n3. Copy text \"B\" inside the Godot editor\n4. Check the clipboard history, still shows \"A\" in the list\n5. Copy text \"C\" outside Godot\n6. Check the clipboard history, now shows \"C\", \"A\" in the list (ordered chronologically)\n7. Copy text \"D\" inside the Godot editor\n8. Check the clipboard history, now shows \"D\", \"C\", \"A\" in the list\n9. Copy text \"E\" inside the Godot editor\n10. Check the clipboard history, shows \"D\", \"C\", \"A\" in the list\n\nDespite not being logged, pasting still works properly (according to the example scenario, it will paste \"E\")\n\nUsing X11 (set `run/platforms/linuxbsd/prefer_wayland` to false) does not seem to have this issue.\n\nNot sure if this is reproducible in other clipboard managers or DEs\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Launch the editor with native Wayland\n2. Copy any text in the editor\n3. Open the clipboard history and observe that the copied text is logged\n4. Copy different text in the editor again\n5. Open the clipboard history again, and observe that the second copy is not logged.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNot needed","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga